WEBVTT

00:00:29.072 --> 00:00:31.117
Apologies for the delay.

00:00:31.161 --> 00:00:34.860
You aren't the only Federation
spy I'm interrogating today.

00:00:34.903 --> 00:00:37.428
Ensign Beckett Mariner!

00:00:37.471 --> 00:00:39.865
Ah, no biggie. I don't have
anything else going on.

00:00:39.908 --> 00:00:41.736
We'll see if you're so cavalier

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.826
after a taste of my...
excruciator!

00:00:47.351 --> 00:00:48.613
Ready to talk?

00:00:48.656 --> 00:00:50.180
Yes.

00:00:50.223 --> 00:00:52.486
It's only been a couple
of months working with my mom,

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.706
instead of behind her back--
the line between mom stuff

00:00:54.749 --> 00:00:56.708
and captain stuff
has gotten real fuzzy.

00:00:56.751 --> 00:00:58.144
Your captain is your mother?

00:00:58.188 --> 00:00:59.798
Yeah, lady,
everybody knows that, keep up!

00:00:59.841 --> 00:01:00.929
I thought
you were good at this.

00:01:04.759 --> 00:01:06.413
I used to sneak away
and do all sorts of little,

00:01:06.457 --> 00:01:08.850
off-the-book side missions
without cluing her in.

00:01:08.894 --> 00:01:11.026
Now that's impossible!

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.072
-She's so happy.

00:01:13.116 --> 00:01:14.856
It's very sweet,
but I am losing my mind.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.815
I don't know how much longer
I can do this.

00:01:17.511 --> 00:01:19.078
-Guards!

00:01:30.045 --> 00:01:32.570
Oh, my God, Mariner,
you got to get me out of here!

00:01:32.613 --> 00:01:35.834
-They keep showing me lights.
-No, I am still mad at you.

00:01:35.877 --> 00:01:37.227
What, for going to the Titan?

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:38.706
But you knew I wanted
to get a promotion.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.143
You're supposed
to be my mentor.

00:01:40.186 --> 00:01:41.492
You snuck off
in the middle of my shift

00:01:41.535 --> 00:01:42.710
without saying goodbye.

00:01:42.754 --> 00:01:44.059
You know
who my best friend is now?

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.149
My mom-- it sucks,
it's like work.

00:01:46.192 --> 00:01:47.933
Look, I'm a hologram, okay?

00:01:47.976 --> 00:01:49.543
I'm sure real Boimler had
his reasons.

00:01:49.587 --> 00:01:51.980
I don't know, maybe,
did you ever... intimidate him?

00:01:52.024 --> 00:01:54.592
-What? No, shut up!
-No, no, no! Mariner?

00:01:54.635 --> 00:01:55.897
Aah!

00:01:55.941 --> 00:01:57.508
You're abandoning
your fellow officer?

00:01:57.551 --> 00:01:59.814
Yeah, well, he did it first.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.602
Stop her!

00:02:04.645 --> 00:02:06.517
Look, I never asked
for special treatment.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.606
That is not my style. I mean,
I won't turn it down, though.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:10.216
Oh, wait, does that make me
a bad person?

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.000
You are an extremely bad person.

00:02:12.044 --> 00:02:14.220
Wow, you are nasty!

00:02:14.264 --> 00:02:16.266
Words can hurt just as much
as torture equipment, all right?

00:02:16.309 --> 00:02:18.181
Good!

00:02:21.445 --> 00:02:23.142
I guess I'll just have
to get used to it, you know?

00:02:23.186 --> 00:02:25.013
Life is all about change.
I just always

00:02:25.057 --> 00:02:26.232
thought she'd kick me out
of Starfleet.

00:02:26.276 --> 00:02:28.321
-You'll never escape!
-Right?

00:02:28.365 --> 00:02:30.280
Oh, wait, you're talking
about the detention center?

00:02:30.323 --> 00:02:32.325
Come on, I'm, like, practically
escaped already, read the room.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:56.610
Oh!

00:02:56.654 --> 00:02:58.308
They're locking weapons!

00:02:58.351 --> 00:02:59.961
-Oh, stop being such a...

00:03:00.005 --> 00:03:02.007
Computer, pause program.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:04.662
What do you want, Jennifer?

00:03:04.705 --> 00:03:06.011
What are you doing?

00:03:06.054 --> 00:03:07.578
Cardio,
plus a little strength training.

00:03:07.621 --> 00:03:10.276
So you work out by staging
Cardassian prison breaks?

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.974
-Yeah, what do you do?
-Uh, yoga.

00:03:13.018 --> 00:03:14.846
-Wow, how unique!
-Whatever.

00:03:14.889 --> 00:03:16.978
Captain wants you
in her ready room.

00:03:17.022 --> 00:03:20.243
Look, I know we're not supposed
to have interpersonal conflict,

00:03:20.286 --> 00:03:22.288
but I really hate that Andorian.

00:03:22.332 --> 00:03:25.204
All right, here we go.
Computer, resume program.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:29.339
What are you--
Why are you squatting?

00:03:29.382 --> 00:03:31.993
We're going to die. Stop that!

00:03:32.037 --> 00:03:34.692
I can't-- it's leg day.

00:04:45.502 --> 00:04:47.721
TheCerritos is finishing

00:04:47.765 --> 00:04:49.984
second contact duties
on Apergos.

00:04:50.028 --> 00:04:52.073
On a personal note, my daughter

00:04:52.117 --> 00:04:54.337
has yet another
side mission request.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:56.295
When I agreed
to give her more autonomy,

00:04:56.339 --> 00:04:59.124
I never realized
how often I would be catering

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:02.562
to her whims.
It's getting a bit old.

00:05:02.606 --> 00:05:05.522
Mom, you don't have to keep a
trinket from every side mission

00:05:05.565 --> 00:05:07.262
we do together.
What even is this?

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.613
That's a gratitude mask from
when you gave root juice

00:05:09.656 --> 00:05:10.701
to the Vornilians.

00:05:10.744 --> 00:05:11.789
Right. Right, right,
right, right.

00:05:11.832 --> 00:05:13.399
Speaking of which...

00:05:13.443 --> 00:05:14.835
I want to do one last thing
before we leave system.

00:05:14.879 --> 00:05:17.316
-Of course you do.
-The capital city is filthy.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.318
They never cleaned up after
their industrial revolution.

00:05:19.362 --> 00:05:21.102
Can I power-wash
a couple buildings?

00:05:21.146 --> 00:05:22.669
I mean, if the locals see
how good it can be,

00:05:22.713 --> 00:05:24.105
maybe they'll start
cleaning up on their own.

00:05:24.149 --> 00:05:25.455
Officially, no.

00:05:25.498 --> 00:05:27.805
Starfleet does not
prioritize aesthetics.

00:05:27.848 --> 00:05:30.155
But as your cool mom,

00:05:30.198 --> 00:05:32.331
-I say go for it.

00:05:32.375 --> 00:05:35.116
The away team is awaiting
your orders, Captain.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.728
Sorry, Commander,
I forgot you were there.

00:05:37.771 --> 00:05:40.165
That does tend to happen
a lot these days.

00:05:40.208 --> 00:05:41.949
The Apergosian high leader
just needs to select

00:05:41.993 --> 00:05:44.604
a subspace communication number
and we'll be good to go.

00:05:44.648 --> 00:05:46.650
Sure, you're authorized
to proceed.

00:05:46.693 --> 00:05:48.478
Oh, and, Jack?

00:05:48.521 --> 00:05:50.436
Make sure Mariner gets
whatever she needs.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:51.611
Yes, sir.

00:05:51.655 --> 00:05:54.092
Thanks, Jack!

00:05:58.183 --> 00:06:00.359
Hey, have you guys seen my PADD?
I just zinged Ransom so hard.

00:06:00.403 --> 00:06:02.187
I got to do a personal log
before I forget.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:04.798
-Did you check Boimler's bunk?

00:06:04.842 --> 00:06:07.322
He'd lose his mind if he knew
we were using this for storage.

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:09.412
He probably has a huge room
to himself on the Titan.

00:06:09.455 --> 00:06:12.197
Yeah, he's probably so excited
about serving with Riker

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.894
he isn't thinking
about us at all.

00:06:13.938 --> 00:06:15.635
-Okey dokey!

00:06:15.679 --> 00:06:18.290
Ensign Barnes just confirmed
our date for tonight.

00:06:18.333 --> 00:06:20.292
Whoa, she's crazy hot!
Are you nervous?

00:06:20.335 --> 00:06:21.772
Wait, that sounds familiar.

00:06:21.815 --> 00:06:23.948
No, not nervous at all.
This is gonna be great.

00:06:23.991 --> 00:06:26.037
Oh, actually, you went on a date
with Barnes last year

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.779
and it wasn't a good match.
She didn't care that a red alert

00:06:28.822 --> 00:06:30.476
failed to override
maintenance hatch 70's

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.260
access protocol--
can you imagine?

00:06:32.304 --> 00:06:34.001
That's okay--
this is our third date.

00:06:34.045 --> 00:06:36.874
It's been pretty great.
Ensign Barnes is super cool.

00:06:36.917 --> 00:06:39.093
Oh! Oh, okay.

00:06:40.312 --> 00:06:42.357
Eh, went the wrong way again.

00:06:42.401 --> 00:06:45.012
Does Rutherford seem off to you?

00:06:45.056 --> 00:06:46.274
Yeah, always. Why?

00:06:46.318 --> 00:06:47.711
Last year, he didn't like pears.

00:06:47.754 --> 00:06:49.713
And now he eats them
all the time.

00:06:49.756 --> 00:06:51.541
I mean, his implant and part
of his brain got ripped out

00:06:51.584 --> 00:06:54.195
of his head and put back in,
so "liking pears"

00:06:54.239 --> 00:06:56.067
doesn't seem
like that big of a deal.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.634
What about Barnes? Three dates?

00:06:57.677 --> 00:06:59.766
-He's not supposed to like her.
-Tendi?

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.376
if Rutherford dating someone
bugs you,

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.856
maybe you should talk to him.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.510
Ha! No, I don't care about that.

00:07:04.554 --> 00:07:07.208
Synthetic Memory Degradation.

00:07:07.252 --> 00:07:08.862
It's a rare condition
that affects cyborgs

00:07:08.906 --> 00:07:10.168
with new implants.

00:07:10.211 --> 00:07:11.691
First your opinions change,

00:07:11.735 --> 00:07:14.520
then your brain liquifies
and melts out of your nose!

00:07:14.564 --> 00:07:16.740
Luckily, this is exactly
what I've been training for.

00:07:16.783 --> 00:07:19.003
I will save my friend!

00:07:19.046 --> 00:07:20.570
Cool.

00:07:20.613 --> 00:07:22.746
So, you really think Boimler has
a big room on the Titan?

00:07:22.789 --> 00:07:24.704
Yeah, it's probably huge.

00:07:31.406 --> 00:07:34.453
Hmm, no. No.

00:07:34.497 --> 00:07:36.107
Ugh. No.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.761
You know,
your communication number

00:07:37.804 --> 00:07:39.545
doesn't really matter,
Your Excellency.

00:07:39.589 --> 00:07:40.851
People just say, "Computer,

00:07:40.894 --> 00:07:42.635
contact the Apergosian High Leader,"

00:07:42.679 --> 00:07:44.811
-and it does it automatically.
-Well, Apergosians have

00:07:44.855 --> 00:07:47.248
a deep relationship
with numbers, Commander.

00:07:47.292 --> 00:07:49.250
It needs to have gravitas--

00:07:49.294 --> 00:07:51.383
digits our grandchildren
can be proud of.

00:07:51.426 --> 00:07:52.993
Yes, yes, right.

00:07:53.037 --> 00:07:55.518
Hey! Look at this one!
This one's got gravitas.

00:07:55.561 --> 00:07:58.085
Mm, too close
to my ex-girlfriend's number.

00:07:58.129 --> 00:08:00.087
I need more options.

00:08:00.131 --> 00:08:03.221
Fine. Mariner, could you
grab me some more PADDs?

00:08:03.264 --> 00:08:04.831
Ooh, no can do. Sorry.

00:08:04.875 --> 00:08:07.181
Sort of busy with, you know,
whatever I feel like doing.

00:08:07.225 --> 00:08:09.140
I'm in command
of this mission, Ensign.

00:08:09.183 --> 00:08:10.445
Get me my PADDs!

00:08:10.489 --> 00:08:13.100
But I am authorized
by the captain

00:08:13.144 --> 00:08:14.580
to do my own mission.

00:08:14.624 --> 00:08:16.277
Have Stevens grab 'em.
He's your little buddy.

00:08:16.321 --> 00:08:18.149
-He is not!
-Here's those PADDs, sir.

00:08:18.192 --> 00:08:19.585
Stacked 'em
just the way you like.

00:08:19.629 --> 00:08:21.848
Get away from me, Stevens.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:33.991
Whoa. I never knew the ancient
ones decorated these buildings.

00:08:34.034 --> 00:08:35.775
You seeing this?

00:08:35.819 --> 00:08:37.821
-Hmm.

00:08:37.864 --> 00:08:39.387
Clean your public spaces,
people.

00:08:39.431 --> 00:08:41.041
It's not that hard.

00:08:41.085 --> 00:08:43.391
Who knows what you'll find
under all this soot?

00:08:51.312 --> 00:08:52.662
Oh!

00:08:52.705 --> 00:08:54.533
Uh, we got sci-fi stuff
happening over here!

00:08:56.666 --> 00:08:58.319
Mariner, get out of there!

00:09:00.539 --> 00:09:03.890
Sir, I'm reading a buildup
of strange energies.

00:09:03.934 --> 00:09:05.892
Mariner! Mariner!

00:09:05.936 --> 00:09:08.416
-Ah!
-Ah!

00:09:09.722 --> 00:09:11.332
Commander?

00:09:11.376 --> 00:09:12.638
Commander, can you hear me?

00:09:12.682 --> 00:09:14.205
Oh, God, is he alive?

00:09:14.248 --> 00:09:15.772
-Please tell me he's alive!

00:09:15.815 --> 00:09:17.469
Calm down, Stevens.
He's gonna be fine.

00:09:17.512 --> 00:09:18.862
Don't lie to me!

00:09:21.734 --> 00:09:24.215
I told you not
to deviate from the mission.

00:09:24.258 --> 00:09:26.609
Hmm. Looks like
you took a full load

00:09:26.652 --> 00:09:28.872
of strange energy
straight to the cortex.

00:09:28.915 --> 00:09:31.048
What is
"strange energy," Doctor?

00:09:31.091 --> 00:09:33.703
Electrical phenomena
with unknown properties.

00:09:33.746 --> 00:09:35.705
It can have all sorts
of physical effects--

00:09:35.748 --> 00:09:39.665
unlock parts of the brain,
even endow god-like powers.

00:09:39.709 --> 00:09:42.059
Humanity has
a complicated relationship

00:09:42.102 --> 00:09:43.669
with organized religion.

00:09:43.713 --> 00:09:45.149
Well, strange energies doesn't.

00:09:45.192 --> 00:09:46.498
Ever hear of Gary Mitchell?

00:09:46.541 --> 00:09:48.500
Uh, it got real weird real fast.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.025
Those energies
weren't that strange. I'm fine.

00:09:52.069 --> 00:09:56.900
Now unhand me. I must rise!

00:09:56.943 --> 00:09:58.379
And he's hovering.

00:09:58.423 --> 00:10:00.207
I think he might be
going god-like on us?

00:10:00.251 --> 00:10:03.210
Let's not jump to conclusions
until I run some tests.

00:10:03.254 --> 00:10:05.125
You mortals tire me!

00:10:06.997 --> 00:10:08.781
Excelsior. I am healed.

00:10:08.825 --> 00:10:10.130
My power swells.

00:10:10.174 --> 00:10:12.655
My brain is unlocking
its full potential.

00:10:12.698 --> 00:10:14.004
Well, lucky for us,

00:10:14.047 --> 00:10:15.179
there isn't much
to unlock in there.

00:10:15.222 --> 00:10:16.702
I can hear your thoughts!

00:10:16.746 --> 00:10:18.443
Uh, I mean, hey,
I was just joking around,

00:10:18.486 --> 00:10:19.923
privately, in-in my head.

00:10:19.966 --> 00:10:22.186
I have to figure out
the right harmonic frequency

00:10:22.229 --> 00:10:23.753
that will disrupt
his power cycle.

00:10:35.939 --> 00:10:37.375
What is he doing now?

00:10:37.418 --> 00:10:38.985
It's easy to become a god.

00:10:39.029 --> 00:10:41.074
The trick is staying a god.

00:10:41.118 --> 00:10:43.729
He seems to be focusing
on his bi's and tri's.

00:10:43.773 --> 00:10:45.731
Captain, we have
an incoming communication

00:10:45.775 --> 00:10:47.037
from Admiral Freeman.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.821
I'll take it in my ready room.

00:10:49.648 --> 00:10:51.868
Hey, sweetheart.
Just checking in on the mission.

00:10:51.911 --> 00:10:54.218
Oh, sorry. Did I catch you
in the middle of something?

00:10:54.261 --> 00:10:57.395
Nah. Just having lunch--
some hot chili.

00:10:57.438 --> 00:10:58.831
No, the mission is great.

00:10:58.875 --> 00:11:00.528
Second contact
is almost complete.

00:11:00.572 --> 00:11:02.487
You know, Carol Bear, you
impressed some important people

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:04.489
with your showdown
with the Pakleds.

00:11:04.532 --> 00:11:06.578
This could be your year to get
promoted to a capital ship--

00:11:06.621 --> 00:11:08.275
as long as you keep
a clean record, of course.

00:11:08.319 --> 00:11:09.755
Oh, the Cerritos?

00:11:09.799 --> 00:11:13.150
Oh, it's the very image
of Starfleet responsibility.

00:11:13.193 --> 00:11:15.630
Mariner,
get Ransom under control

00:11:15.674 --> 00:11:17.894
and get that number picked now!

00:11:17.937 --> 00:11:19.591
Yelling at me
isn't going to help!

00:11:19.634 --> 00:11:21.941
Oh, yeah. Feel the burn!

00:11:23.377 --> 00:11:25.771
So, wait. My brain's gonna melt
out of my nose

00:11:25.815 --> 00:11:27.120
because I like pears?

00:11:27.164 --> 00:11:28.687
No, no, no, no, no.

00:11:28.731 --> 00:11:30.167
There's a problem in the way
that your hippocampus

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.908
and your implant
are communicating.

00:11:31.951 --> 00:11:33.605
Okay, so what's
with all the disks?

00:11:33.648 --> 00:11:34.911
They provide a low-level shock.

00:11:34.954 --> 00:11:36.695
A shock? There's, like,
a hundred of 'em!

00:11:36.739 --> 00:11:39.132
Reacting to pain can often kick
neurons right back into place.

00:11:39.176 --> 00:11:41.134
Wait. How much pain? Aah!

00:11:41.178 --> 00:11:42.919
That kind of hurt!
Can you warn me next time?

00:11:42.962 --> 00:11:44.355
Uh, sorry, I can't.

00:11:44.398 --> 00:11:45.791
The shocks have to come
at unexpected times.

00:11:45.835 --> 00:11:47.488
-I can't tell you when I'm...

00:11:47.532 --> 00:11:48.751
That one was worse!

00:11:48.794 --> 00:11:49.795
I have to randomize
the voltage,

00:11:49.839 --> 00:11:50.796
or your brain will tune it out.

00:11:51.971 --> 00:11:53.668
Do you still like pears?

00:11:53.712 --> 00:11:55.105
Yes!

00:11:57.107 --> 00:11:58.586
Huh?

00:11:58.630 --> 00:11:59.892
How about now?

00:11:59.936 --> 00:12:01.285
Uh, pears? No, I hate pears.

00:12:01.328 --> 00:12:02.808
I'll never eat a pear again.

00:12:02.852 --> 00:12:04.157
Then you should
pass this test.

00:12:04.201 --> 00:12:06.246
Three sets of twins are lost
at sea.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:08.292
Each set shares a parent
with the other,

00:12:08.335 --> 00:12:10.076
but no two sets are the same.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:12.862
What is the name of the boat?

00:12:12.905 --> 00:12:16.648
Uh, um... The Salty Dog?

00:12:16.691 --> 00:12:17.954
-Yes!
-Really?

00:12:17.997 --> 00:12:19.956
-No.

00:12:19.999 --> 00:12:21.827
No, what are you doing?
No, don't do that!

00:12:21.871 --> 00:12:23.394
-I'm late for my date.
-But your brain!

00:12:23.437 --> 00:12:25.439
Was feeling great
until you started shocking me.

00:12:25.483 --> 00:12:27.180
This isn't like you!

00:12:27.224 --> 00:12:31.228
Looks like I'm going to have to
resort to more extreme methods.

00:12:37.843 --> 00:12:40.063
That displeases Ransom.

00:12:41.238 --> 00:12:43.153
He made the moon disappear.

00:12:43.196 --> 00:12:44.545
Hey, buddy, look at...
look at this.

00:12:44.589 --> 00:12:46.156
-This... this might be

00:12:46.199 --> 00:12:47.897
the best subspace number
I've even seen.

00:12:50.508 --> 00:12:53.424
He just ruined our museum
of popular music!

00:12:53.467 --> 00:12:55.513
Hey, that sounds
like something you don't need.

00:12:55.556 --> 00:12:57.863
Mom, I don't think
this is going to happen.

00:12:57.907 --> 00:12:59.517
Well, it has to!

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:02.476
I never should have authorized
you to break mission parameters.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:04.000
Well, how was I supposed to know
this was all gonna go

00:13:04.043 --> 00:13:05.305
all Ransom on the mount?

00:13:05.349 --> 00:13:08.656
I will create a race
of Ransomites!

00:13:12.225 --> 00:13:14.662
Hey, don't transform
my constituents!

00:13:14.706 --> 00:13:16.186
Ooh, ooh, do me, sir!

00:13:16.229 --> 00:13:18.101
it. I'm gonna blast him.

00:13:18.144 --> 00:13:20.146
No! Shooting
from the hip is what

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.887
landed us here
in the first place.

00:13:21.931 --> 00:13:23.367
Just calm him down.

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:25.717
Mom, I feel that you are not
listening to me.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:27.545
I am going to calm him down...
by blasting him.

00:13:27.588 --> 00:13:30.200
When you say that,
what I hear is

00:13:30.243 --> 00:13:33.072
that you don't like
being disagreed with.

00:13:36.946 --> 00:13:39.209
Ah!

00:13:40.601 --> 00:13:42.299
Ah, damn it!

00:13:44.301 --> 00:13:45.650
We have to be a team on this.

00:13:45.693 --> 00:13:47.565
Yeah, no. Of course,
yeah, love to be a team.

00:13:47.608 --> 00:13:49.654
Stop pretending
to like each other.

00:13:49.697 --> 00:13:52.396
It's making me furious!

00:13:52.439 --> 00:13:55.051
I am superior to all of you!

00:13:55.094 --> 00:13:57.444
Oh, it's true.
All hail Ransom.

00:13:57.488 --> 00:13:59.794
I bow.
I bow before thee, sir.

00:13:59.838 --> 00:14:02.841
Emergency transport to sickbay
for Commander Ransom now.

00:14:05.757 --> 00:14:07.411
Dude, not cool!

00:14:07.454 --> 00:14:09.195
Doc, how did they deal
with Gary Mitchell?

00:14:09.239 --> 00:14:10.936
Kirk smooshed him
with a boulder.

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:14.070
Gary Mitchell was an ant,
and I am a lion!

00:14:21.338 --> 00:14:22.817
You know what?

00:14:22.861 --> 00:14:24.732
Maybe we shouldn't be
seeing each other tonight.

00:14:24.776 --> 00:14:27.126
My memory's all messed up
because of my new implant.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.736
Sorry if I say anything weird.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.216
Don't worry. I'm used to it.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.957
My older sister got a symbiont,

00:14:32.001 --> 00:14:33.611
and it totally
changed her personality.

00:14:33.654 --> 00:14:35.395
Oh, is it because she has all
the memories and experiences

00:14:35.439 --> 00:14:37.093
-of her past lives in her head?
-Meh.

00:14:37.136 --> 00:14:39.965
It's more that she always has
to bring up having a symbiont.

00:14:40.009 --> 00:14:41.445
It's like, we get it.

00:14:41.488 --> 00:14:43.795
-When are you back on duty?

00:14:43.838 --> 00:14:45.971
Me and a couple girls from
cetacean ops are going swimming.

00:14:46.015 --> 00:14:47.277
Want to join?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.018
Sure. This thing is waterproof.

00:14:49.061 --> 00:14:50.889
-I can swim all night.
-Great.

00:14:50.933 --> 00:14:53.065
Uh, I think your friend
is gonna shoot you.

00:14:53.109 --> 00:14:55.502
What now?

00:14:55.546 --> 00:14:57.461
-Tendi, what are you doing?!
-Sorry to interrupt,

00:14:57.504 --> 00:14:59.463
but I really don't want you
to die again!

00:14:59.506 --> 00:15:02.161
-Hi. I'm Tendi. We're friends.
-Nice to meet you.

00:15:02.205 --> 00:15:03.815
Tendi, come on!
You don't have to do this!

00:15:03.858 --> 00:15:06.905
I'm in medical, he has SMD,
I'm just saving his life.

00:15:06.949 --> 00:15:08.298
What's an SMD?

00:15:08.341 --> 00:15:11.823
It's just a cyborg thing.
I'm fine. Aah! Uh.

00:15:11.866 --> 00:15:13.129
Well, when you're cured,

00:15:13.172 --> 00:15:14.565
just meet us
outside cetacean ops.

00:15:14.608 --> 00:15:16.175
I'm going
to go change into my swimsuit.

00:15:16.219 --> 00:15:18.134
Wait, wait, wait, wait!
I can come with you!

00:15:18.177 --> 00:15:20.136
Oh, no, you can't!

00:15:20.179 --> 00:15:21.267
What's in those hyposprays?

00:15:21.311 --> 00:15:22.660
Medical venom!

00:15:22.703 --> 00:15:23.922
Ugh. Stop!

00:15:23.966 --> 00:15:25.315
You can't just
keep attacking me and trying

00:15:25.358 --> 00:15:26.664
to surprise me
into getting better.

00:15:26.707 --> 00:15:28.971
-If I do have this LSD thing...
-SMD.

00:15:29.014 --> 00:15:31.625
Whatever. You can't cure it
like getting rid of hiccups.

00:15:31.669 --> 00:15:34.498
You're right.
-Thank you.

00:15:34.541 --> 00:15:36.369
I'll have to get your brain
out of your skull

00:15:36.413 --> 00:15:38.850
and freeze it so I can nano
suture your dendrites by hand.

00:15:38.893 --> 00:15:41.374
Tendi, please! I just want
to go swimming with girls!

00:15:41.418 --> 00:15:43.855
-Then give me your brain!
-No!

00:15:43.898 --> 00:15:46.423
My will be done!

00:15:46.466 --> 00:15:49.817
Behold the first coming
of Ransom!

00:15:49.861 --> 00:15:52.168
Captain, there's a giant head
approaching the ship.

00:15:52.211 --> 00:15:54.039
Red alert. Evasive action.

00:16:02.395 --> 00:16:04.528
Is this gym equipment?

00:16:04.571 --> 00:16:07.183
He's creating his own
Jack utopia.

00:16:10.186 --> 00:16:13.058
Wait.
If we can't nullify his powers,

00:16:13.102 --> 00:16:14.581
we should boost them.

00:16:14.625 --> 00:16:16.235
Why the hell would we do that?

00:16:16.279 --> 00:16:18.585
There's a chance it could
short out his godliness.

00:16:18.629 --> 00:16:20.935
Yeah,
or make him extra vengeful.

00:16:20.979 --> 00:16:22.459
Aah!

00:16:22.502 --> 00:16:24.069
Oh, what,
you have a better idea?

00:16:24.113 --> 00:16:27.377
Mom, hit that head
with everything you've got.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:29.335
Doc says it'll overload him.

00:16:32.295 --> 00:16:35.733
Oh, yes, feed me your phasers.
I can feel

00:16:35.776 --> 00:16:39.302
myself becoming more powerful
than ever before!

00:16:39.345 --> 00:16:42.174
More power
just gave him more power!

00:16:42.218 --> 00:16:43.958
I have to reason with him.

00:16:44.002 --> 00:16:45.482
Open a channel.

00:16:45.525 --> 00:16:48.180
Why are you doing this, Jack?
Stand down.

00:16:48.224 --> 00:16:51.401
I used to be your number one,
but then Mariner took it all

00:16:51.444 --> 00:16:53.751
just because
she's your daughter.

00:16:53.794 --> 00:16:56.536
Then from now on,
you can work with us, too.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:58.495
I don't want to work with her!

00:17:05.632 --> 00:17:08.374
Stay away from me. I want
my brain right where it is.

00:17:08.418 --> 00:17:09.984
I'm just borrowing it.
I-I'll give it right back.

00:17:10.028 --> 00:17:11.943
Computer, activate force field,

00:17:11.986 --> 00:17:13.423
-Corridor 755.

00:17:13.466 --> 00:17:15.294
I'm trying to save you.

00:17:15.338 --> 00:17:16.774
I don't need to be saved.

00:17:16.817 --> 00:17:17.949
But we're best friends!

00:17:17.992 --> 00:17:19.429
We have to trust each other.

00:17:19.472 --> 00:17:21.126
Well, then,
maybe we shouldn't be friends.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.917
You don't have
Synthetic Memory Degradation.

00:17:29.961 --> 00:17:31.267
What?!

00:17:34.357 --> 00:17:35.619
Mom,

00:17:35.662 --> 00:17:37.229
hit him with photon torpedoes.

00:17:37.273 --> 00:17:38.970
Don't you give me orders.

00:17:39.013 --> 00:17:41.146
-I thought we were partners.
Lies.

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:42.452
You hate working together!

00:17:42.495 --> 00:17:44.976
That's not true. Right, Mom?

00:17:45.019 --> 00:17:46.282
I, uh...

00:17:46.325 --> 00:17:48.240
He's right.

00:17:48.284 --> 00:17:50.460
What? Well, I do...

00:17:50.503 --> 00:17:52.070
actually feel
the exact same way.

00:17:52.114 --> 00:17:53.637
I hate being your sidekick.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.205
And I hate the way
you question me all the time.

00:17:56.248 --> 00:18:00.122
You're both fakers! And now
you'll pay the ultimate price!

00:18:24.058 --> 00:18:25.364
You don't have SMD,

00:18:25.408 --> 00:18:27.236
but there's definitely
something wrong with you.

00:18:27.279 --> 00:18:30.195
If you knew I wasn't in danger,
then why were you hunting me?

00:18:30.239 --> 00:18:31.892
Well, you changed your opinion
on so many things,

00:18:31.936 --> 00:18:33.764
I was worried
that if I didn't do something,

00:18:33.807 --> 00:18:36.897
you might decide
you didn't like me anymore, too.

00:18:36.941 --> 00:18:39.465
I'm a monster.
I shouldn't be your doctor.

00:18:39.509 --> 00:18:41.380
So, you were utilizing

00:18:41.424 --> 00:18:43.861
highly invasive
neuro-medical procedures

00:18:43.904 --> 00:18:47.125
in order to make sure
I liked you?

00:18:47.169 --> 00:18:49.562
Yes. You can hate me.

00:18:49.606 --> 00:18:52.174
Computer,
deactivate force field.

00:18:52.217 --> 00:18:53.958
Ha! How could I hate you?

00:18:54.001 --> 00:18:56.743
Tackling an emotional problem
with scientific experimentation

00:18:56.787 --> 00:18:58.397
is exactly
what I would have done.

00:18:58.441 --> 00:18:59.877
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.487
But you don't have to,
'cause guess what?

00:19:01.531 --> 00:19:04.316
No new implant is gonna stop me
from being your friend.

00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:06.100
Aw. Thanks, Rutherford.

00:19:06.144 --> 00:19:07.667
It's nice to know
no matter what,

00:19:07.711 --> 00:19:09.321
we still love science.

00:19:09.365 --> 00:19:11.062
And how.

00:19:11.105 --> 00:19:12.890
Also, don't date Barnes.

00:19:18.548 --> 00:19:20.245
He's growing hands.

00:19:20.289 --> 00:19:21.942
Brace for grabbing!

00:19:23.161 --> 00:19:24.554
Shoot him

00:19:24.597 --> 00:19:26.251
with the dang torpedoes already!

00:19:26.295 --> 00:19:27.600
And I'm gonna go find a boulder.

00:19:27.644 --> 00:19:30.124
-No! Power down weapons.
-But Captain!

00:19:30.168 --> 00:19:32.779
I'm not shooting
my friend anymore.

00:19:32.823 --> 00:19:34.172
Why not?

00:19:34.216 --> 00:19:35.434
Because you're right.

00:19:35.478 --> 00:19:37.480
Mariner and I
haven't been honest,

00:19:37.523 --> 00:19:39.003
and you got caught
in the middle.

00:19:39.046 --> 00:19:40.787
You're a great officer, Jack.

00:19:40.831 --> 00:19:42.920
I shouldn't have taken you
for granted.

00:19:42.963 --> 00:19:45.444
Captain, his power is...
diminishing.

00:19:45.488 --> 00:19:48.317
Your validation feels so good.

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:49.622
Tell me more.

00:19:49.666 --> 00:19:51.537
I can end this with praise.

00:19:51.581 --> 00:19:54.279
Uh, J-Jack,
you're a-a fine commander.

00:19:54.323 --> 00:19:55.933
You're in phenomenal shape.

00:19:55.976 --> 00:19:58.936
Yes, fine commander.
Yes, so yoked.

00:19:58.979 --> 00:20:00.807
Mom, you've got to hit him.
He's a god.

00:20:00.851 --> 00:20:02.592
You can't appeal
to his ego forever.

00:20:02.635 --> 00:20:04.942
Stand down, Ensign.
I've got this.

00:20:04.985 --> 00:20:08.989
Jack, you're an amazing pilot,
a-a brilliant tactician and...

00:20:09.033 --> 00:20:11.557
Oh, you're right.
I should be captain!

00:20:11.601 --> 00:20:12.906
Yeah, well,
I don't know about that.

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:14.821
-Why not?
-That position is filled.

00:20:14.865 --> 00:20:16.823
We can't have two captains.

00:20:16.867 --> 00:20:19.043
Not two. Just me.

00:20:19.086 --> 00:20:21.524
Full stop, mister.
This is my ship.

00:20:21.567 --> 00:20:23.308
I want to be the captain!

00:20:27.312 --> 00:20:28.531
Wait, Jack, no!

00:20:28.574 --> 00:20:29.749
You've got great hair,

00:20:29.793 --> 00:20:31.316
and you're so good
at guitar and...

00:20:33.057 --> 00:20:36.190
What? It worked?
Was it the guitar thing?

00:20:36.234 --> 00:20:37.279
Uh...

00:20:37.322 --> 00:20:40.412
I'm going to destroy you...

00:20:42.893 --> 00:20:45.504
What the hell is happening
down there?

00:20:45.548 --> 00:20:47.332
Ow!

00:20:47.376 --> 00:20:50.074
Sorry, Mom. I had to take
matters into my own feet.

00:20:59.388 --> 00:21:00.954
Mariner? What was I doing?

00:21:00.998 --> 00:21:02.565
You were trying
to eat the ship, sir.

00:21:02.608 --> 00:21:04.828
I had to apply concentrated
force to your neutral zone.

00:21:04.871 --> 00:21:06.569
I'm sorry.
Those strange energies

00:21:06.612 --> 00:21:07.744
may have given me powers,

00:21:07.787 --> 00:21:09.528
but it was my ego
that turned me...

00:21:09.572 --> 00:21:11.661
into a monster!

00:21:11.704 --> 00:21:13.227
Sorry. Your eyes were glowing.

00:21:13.271 --> 00:21:15.012
Thank you. I could feel myself

00:21:15.055 --> 00:21:18.058
succumbing to the power.

00:21:18.102 --> 00:21:19.321
Would you stop it, Beckett?

00:21:19.364 --> 00:21:20.322
No can do.

00:21:34.727 --> 00:21:36.076
Oh!

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:39.166
Here, I picked a number.
Just go.

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:42.256
No!

00:21:43.345 --> 00:21:45.564
TheCerritos is on its way

00:21:45.608 --> 00:21:47.261
to the Bitrus Expanse,

00:21:47.305 --> 00:21:49.786
and Commander Ransom
should make a full recovery.

00:21:49.829 --> 00:21:51.396
I'm really sorry

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:52.919
about the whole omniscient
murder-god thing, Captain.

00:21:52.963 --> 00:21:54.921
Well, you just focus
on getting better.

00:21:54.965 --> 00:21:57.750
I need you by my side.

00:21:58.490 --> 00:21:59.926
All right, big guy.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:01.667
Today, I'll be reading you
"Nightingale Woman."

00:22:01.711 --> 00:22:03.582
Thanks, little buddy.

00:22:03.626 --> 00:22:05.758
Hey, Mom. How's Ransom?

00:22:05.802 --> 00:22:08.282
He's fine.
Stevens hasn't left his side.

00:22:08.326 --> 00:22:10.067
You know, it was cool

00:22:10.110 --> 00:22:12.417
being an unstoppable
mommy-daughter team for a while,

00:22:12.461 --> 00:22:14.637
but I think
maybe we work better apart.

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:16.943
Agreed.
I'm proud you're my daughter,

00:22:16.987 --> 00:22:20.077
but I can't stand
sharing command with you.

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:21.513
Hey, maybe from now on,

00:22:21.557 --> 00:22:23.297
we only do
some side missions together.

00:22:23.341 --> 00:22:24.647
I would like that.

00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:26.126
There's a team

00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:27.780
waiting to take me to the brig,
isn't there?

00:22:27.824 --> 00:22:30.435
-Ah, you know me so well.

00:22:30.479 --> 00:22:32.132
Love you, Mom.

00:22:32.176 --> 00:22:35.309
Love you, too.
Never disobey me again.

00:22:35.353 --> 00:22:37.094
I do what I want!

00:22:37.921 --> 00:22:40.140
So, your brains
aren't going to melt?

00:22:40.184 --> 00:22:41.620
Nope.
I mean, not from the implant.

00:22:41.664 --> 00:22:43.013
But we're in Starfleet,

00:22:43.056 --> 00:22:44.406
so who knows
what's gonna happen next week.

00:22:44.449 --> 00:22:45.885
We worked together
and managed to revert

00:22:45.929 --> 00:22:47.409
one of his synaptic pathways.

00:22:47.452 --> 00:22:49.323
-Oh, that's nice. Which one?
-I hate pears again.

00:22:49.367 --> 00:22:52.326
They're so mealy and bland.
pears.

00:22:52.370 --> 00:22:54.328
Well, it seems like
everything's back to normal.

00:22:54.372 --> 00:22:56.766
Yeah.
Only thing missing is Boimler.

00:22:56.809 --> 00:22:58.420
I do miss the guy,
but I can't blame him.

00:22:58.463 --> 00:22:59.986
I mean,
think of all the fun adventures

00:23:00.030 --> 00:23:01.466
he's going on working with Riker

00:23:01.510 --> 00:23:03.555
on a ship that's way cooler
than the Cerritos.

00:23:03.599 --> 00:23:05.209
It's everything he ever wanted.

00:23:05.252 --> 00:23:08.473
He's got to be having
the time of his life.

00:23:16.089 --> 00:23:18.309
Shields at 30%!
-Red alert!

00:23:18.352 --> 00:23:19.919
I'm starting to think
this jam session's

00:23:19.963 --> 00:23:22.052
got too many licks
and not enough comp.

00:23:22.095 --> 00:23:24.184
What does that even mean?!

00:23:24.228 --> 00:23:26.578
More Pakled battle harpies
just dropped out of warp!

00:23:26.622 --> 00:23:27.666
They've got us surrounded!

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:28.711
Someone punch me a way out.

00:23:28.754 --> 00:23:29.799
Punching.

00:23:29.842 --> 00:23:32.192
I'm taking us into the anomaly.

00:23:32.236 --> 00:23:35.021
-Brace for gluonic disruption.
-Gluonic what?!

00:23:38.285 --> 00:23:40.897
I love my job!
